                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TL, DR: Fun game, but not much content. For like 3€ you can have one hour easy puzzling, but nothing more. 15€ is far too expensive for the content!\n\nLike other reviewers said, the game is a bit like Lemmings: you have to get your astroderps to the goal, while they wander mindlessly into certain death or jump off of cliffs - thus the title lemmings. Instead of manipulating the astroderps directly, you change blocks and stairs and form a way for the astroderps. \n\nMost of the levels are fairly easy. The art style, the controls and the sound are okay, but nothing more.\n\nOnly the amount of content is really frustrating - there are few level and I finished the game in under 1 hour! That's not enough playtime for a complete game. The price/content proportion is a no go and I can understand, when other players won't recommend the game because of this. But the game itself is okay, so I will give it a recommendation - but only barely and only if it's on sale.",
